2-16","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828025057323/0001628280-25-057323-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-12-11","form":"8-K","codes":["5.07"],"events":[{"label":"Shareholder vote results","kind":"governance","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000178635225000043/0001786352-25-000043-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-11-06","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828025050144/0001628280-25-050144-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-10-20","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828025045516/0001628280-25-045516-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["BILL Holdings, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Services-Prepackaged Software\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 6 years.","It reported $1.6bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 13.5% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 81.6%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($257.2m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 13.5% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $406.6m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Gross margin of 81.6% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $257.2m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828025050328/0001628280-25-050328-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-25-050328"}],"bear":[{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-0.1% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 10.2% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 8.9% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (32,875 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000206742526000001/0002067425-26-000001-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.3% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000206742526000001/0002067425-26-000001-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 74.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.74,"consecutive":2,"current":0.816,"current_display":"81.6%","threshold_display":"74.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -2.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.02,"consecutive":2,"current":0.135,"current_display":"13.5%","threshold_display":"-2.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 17.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.17,"consecutive":1,"current":0.102,"current_display":"10.2%","threshold_display":"17.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.483,"current_display":"0.48","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive t